{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerMathlibFiller","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerMathlibFiller","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Vol_Borromean_eq_two_BW_octahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Vol_Borromean_eq_two_BW_octahedron","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerMathlibFiller.lean#L96-L106","doc":"**Identity: `Vol(B_3) = 2 · BW_Borromean_per_octahedron`.**\n\nVia the 2-octahedra decomposition of the Borromean rings\ncomplement, each octahedron contributing `4G = 4 Cl_2(π/2)`.\nSorry-free by definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Vol_figure_8_eq_two_BW_tetrahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Vol_figure_8_eq_two_BW_tetrahedron","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerMathlibFiller.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**Identity: `Vol(4_1) = 2 · BW_figure_8_per_tetrahedron`.**\n\nDirect combination of the Thurston 2-tetrahedra triangulation\nwith the BW dilogarithm formula. Sorry-free by definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_Borromean_per_octahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_Borromean_per_octahedron","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerMathlibFiller.lean#L76-L83","doc":"**Borromean per-octahedron BW value:** the regular ideal\noctahedron decomposes into 4 ideal tetrahedra of shape\nparameter `i = e^{iπ/2}`, each contributing\n`D(i) = Cl_2(π/2) = G` (Catalan constant). The\nper-octahedron BW value is therefore `4 · Cl_2(π/2) = 4G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_figure_8_per_tetrahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_figure_8_per_tetrahedron","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerMathlibFiller.lean#L68-L74","doc":"**Figure-8 BW value carrier:** `D(e^{iπ/3}) = Cl_2(π/3)`. The\nshape parameter `e^{iπ/3}` is the regular ideal tetrahedron\nrealising the 2-tetrahedra triangulation of the figure-8 knot\ncomplement (Thurston 1978). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle_zero","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerMathlibFiller.lean#L62-L66","doc":"**Boundary lemma:** `D(e^{i · 0}) = D(1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_unit_circle","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerMathlibFiller.lean#L55-L60","doc":"The **Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm restricted to the unit circle**:\nfor `z = e^{iθ}` with `|z| = 1`, the boundary correction\n`log|z| · arg(1-z)` vanishes, leaving\n`D(e^{iθ}) = Im(Li_2(e^{iθ})) = Cl_2(θ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}